cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or results, please cite it as below."
title: "Federated Single-Cell Variational Inference (scVI) with Flower"
authors:
  - family-names: Sommaruga
    given-names: Tommaso
    email: tommaso.sommaruga@student.supsi.ch
repository-code: "https://github.com/tommasosommaruga/SCVI"
license: CC-BY-4.0
year: 2025
type: software
abstract: >-
  Thesis project implementing centralized, independent-client, and federated
  training of scVI (scvi-tools) on pancreas scRNA-seq data using the Flower
  federated learning framework, including federated highly variable gene (HVG)
  selection and evaluation via loss curves, UMAP, and clustering metrics.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - scVI
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - Flower
  - variational autoencoder
  - highly variable genes
